		which is smaller than the exceptional term below under the bootstrap smallness assumption. We now record the three remaining regular pieces in \eqref{eq:gneq0-gradient-explicit} explicitly. First, the two-level zero--wave estimate, the two derivative norms in \eqref{eq:R1-time-complete}, \eqref{eq:roll-recovery-final}, and \eqref{eq:E6-recovery-low}--\eqref{eq:E6-recovery-high} give
		\begin{align}
			\|(\nabla q)\partial_yu^3_{0}\|_{L^2}
			&\leq C\|\partial_yu^3_{0}\|_{H^1}\|\nabla q\|_{L^2}
			+C\|\partial_yu^3_{0}\|_{L^2}\|\nabla q\|_{H^1}
			\nonumber\\
			&\leq C\bigl(\|\nabla_\perp u^\perp_{0}(t)\|_{H^1}+\|\nabla_\perp D_z^V u^\perp_{0}(t)\|_{H^1}\bigr)\mathcal U_{0}+C E_{2}\mathcal U_1.
